    "result": "## Summary\n\nI've successfully fixed the bug where `frai gate init --ci` was not creating the GitHub Actions workflow file. \n\n**The Problem:**\nThe `frai-cli` package was not properly passing the `--ci` flag to the underlying `frai-gate` CLI. This was due to how Commander.js handles variadic arguments with unknown options.\n\n**The Solution:**\nChanged the gate command handler in `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` (lines 737-759) to:\n1. Remove the incorrect parameter handling that only captured partial arguments\n2. Instead, extract all arguments directly from `process.argv` after the 'gate' command\n3. Pass the complete argument list (including all flags) to the spawned gate CLI process\n\n**Verification:**\n- Rebuilt the frai package with `pnpm --filter frai build`\n- Tested `frai gate init --ci` in a fresh directory\n- Confirmed that both `FRAI-SPEC.md` and `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` are now created as expected\n\nThe fix ensures that all flags and options passed to the `gate` command are properly forwarded to the underlying `frai-gate` CLI.",
